  "metadata": {
    "job": "Six-up nested sheet",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "Order is the whole lesson: every hole is bored while its part is still attached, and all six outlines are profiled last, so the sheet stays rigid as long as possible and there is one tool change instead of six. Every part keeps four tabs. The 8mm gap has to clear the ⌀3 cutter — tighten it and profile-collision fires."
  },
